{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Heat shrink tubing complements my earlier wire connectors by helping insulate electrical repairs, giving me a clear reason to choose it.",
    "The black Gorilla outdoor duct tape closely matches tape I have bought before and offers a plausible use for outdoor repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Hose clamps do not mean I need O-ring lubricant, and my vinyl cement purchase does not mean a plastic bonder would suit the material I need to repair.",
    "Ten tubes of super glue and a two-pack of maintenance spray would add supplies without a clear current use. The nut assortment also needs a specific fastening task and matching sizes."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair purchases seem to be treated as interest in almost any maintenance supply, even when each product solves a different problem.",
    "My Gorilla tape purchases seem to count too strongly toward interest in other Gorilla products, although glue serves a different purpose and ten tubes would be excessive for me."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I care about the particular material, connection, and repair task; a related product is useful only when it fits those details.",
    "A complementary supply can be more useful than another kit I may still have. I would check my connector supply before replacing it, while heat shrink tubing adds a distinct function."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical repair interests but sometimes confuse a related supply with something I have a reason to buy now."
}"}
